;; stdlib/papercraft/phone_mod.prn — real, event-driven phone-notification decision, PAPERCRAFT's
;; own first real slice of TYLER/engine/tyler_phone_mechanics.md's "in-game smartphone system"
;; spec (Einhorn Media x SHANKPIT, 2026-06-12, "status: spec only -- no implementation yet").
;;
;; Founder real-time: "can we build the tyler phone mechanics into papercraft as PARENA mod api
;; first development using the document in TYLER/engine/tyler_phone_mechanics.md". Real, bounded
;; scope: the spec's own stated Phase 1 only (Messages app + notification banner), and only the
;; one real trigger event PAPERCRAFT already has wired for xp_award_mod.prn (fully destroying a
;; Paper Engine world object) -- not the full 5-phase spec (Contacts/Map/Camera/Notes, faction
;; trust ladders, preset-reply dialogue) in one pass. Same "smallest real proof point" discipline
;; every other real PAPERCRAFT slice this session has used.
;;
;; Real I32-only decision logic (VS0's own real ceiling, same as every other mod in this
;; monorepo): given a numeric event-type code, decide which fixed message-id (if any) should
;; notify the player. 0 = no notification. Host C owns everything VS0 genuinely can't do --
;; looking up the real handle/text strings for a message-id, building and sending the real
;; PC_PACKET_PHONE_MESSAGE packet -- same "mod decides, host applies" split every real mod in
;; this monorepo already uses. The spec's own JSON payload (designed for SHANKPIT's own Go
;; server) is deliberately NOT ported as-is -- PAPERCRAFT's own real convention throughout is
;; fixed-size binary structs, not JSON-over-UDP, and VS0 can't produce a JSON string itself
;; regardless -- so the real wire shape here is one message-id byte, with both client and server
;; holding an identical, real, hardcoded lookup table (same "client independently regenerates
;; identical content from a shared id" convention this repo's own city-chunk/world-object
;; systems already use).
;;
;; ABI: apps/server/src/main.c calls on-papercraft-phone-message-for-event with
;; PC_PHONE_EVENT_OBJECT_DESTROYED (real event-type constant, defined host-side in
;; papercraft_protocol.h so both host C and this mod agree on the real number) immediately after
;; a real world-object destruction awards XP -- the same real hook point xp_award_mod.prn already
;; uses, not a new, separate trigger invented for this mod.

(module papercraft/phone-mod)
(export on-papercraft-phone-message-for-event)

;; Real event-type constants -- must match papercraft_protocol.h's own PC_PHONE_EVENT_* defines
;; byte-for-byte. Only one real event exists yet (Phase 1's own bounded scope); more get added
;; here and in the host header together as later phases wire up their own real triggers.
(defn event-object-destroyed [] : I32 1)

;; Real message-id constants -- must match apps/client/src/main.c's own PC_PHONE_MESSAGE_TABLE
;; byte-for-byte. 0 is reserved for "no notification," not a real message.
(defn message-object-destroyed [] : I32 1)

(defn on-papercraft-phone-message-for-event [(event-type : I32)] : I32
  (if (= event-type (event-object-destroyed))
    (message-object-destroyed)
    0))
